# 2. Stakeholders and Their Concerns

Stakeholders are the people or systems that are interested in the WordPress CMS. Each stakeholder has different concerns related to usability, security, performance, maintainability, and system reliability.

| Stakeholder | Description | Main Concerns |
|---|---|---|
| Site Visitor | A user who visits the public website to read content. | Fast page loading, easy navigation, mobile-friendly design, secure browsing. |
| Content Author | A user who creates and edits posts, pages, and media content. | Easy content editing, media upload, draft saving, content scheduling, simple dashboard. |
| Site Administrator | A user responsible for managing the complete WordPress website. | User management, role permissions, plugin/theme control, backups, security, updates. |
| Plugin Developer | A developer who creates or installs plugins to extend system functionality. | Clear plugin hooks, compatibility, safe extension points, minimal conflicts with core system. |
| Website Owner / Business Owner | The person or organization that owns the website. | Low cost, business growth, reliability, SEO, analytics, customer engagement. |
| Hosting Provider | Provides server infrastructure for running WordPress. | Server performance, uptime, resource usage, scalability, secure hosting environment. |
| Security Team | Responsible for protecting the website from attacks. | Authentication, authorization, malware protection, secure plugins, backup and recovery. |
| End Customer / Reader | A person who consumes website information or uses website services. | Accurate content, privacy, trust, fast response time, simple user experience. |

