# 3. Key Drivers of the Project

Architecture drivers are the important factors that influence the design of the WordPress CMS architecture. These drivers help the team decide which architecture style, technologies, and design decisions should be used.

| Key Driver | Description | Architectural Impact |
|---|---|---|
| Easy Content Management | Users should be able to create, edit, and publish content without advanced programming skills. | Requires an admin dashboard, editor, media library, and content management module. |
| Extensibility | The system should support new features without changing the core system. | Requires plugin-based architecture and hook/filter mechanisms. |
| Customizable Design | Website appearance should be easily changed. | Requires a theme engine and template-based rendering. |
| Security | The system must protect user accounts, admin access, content, and database. | Requires authentication, RBAC, input validation, HTTPS, backups, and monitoring. |
| Performance | Website pages should load quickly for visitors. | Requires caching, CDN support, optimized database queries, and media optimization. |
| Scalability | The system should handle increasing users and website traffic. | Requires load balancing, multiple WordPress instances, shared storage, and database optimization. |
| Maintainability | The system should be easy to update, manage, and debug. | Requires modular structure, clear separation between core, plugins, themes, and database. |
| Reliability | The website should remain available and recover quickly after failure. | Requires backups, monitoring, database recovery, and redundant deployment. |
| Usability | Non-technical users should easily use the system. | Requires a user-friendly dashboard, clear navigation, and responsive interface. |

